// v15.14: how long to wait after a retryable failure. Named and lifted out of geminiRequest
// so it can be exercised against real 429 bodies instead of only in production.
//
// The Retry-After branch had never once fired. The generativelanguage v1beta endpoint does
// not send that header — it returns the wait inside the error BODY as a google.rpc.RetryInfo
// detail ("retryDelay":"37s"). So every 429 fell through to blind exponential backoff, which
// either over-waits or retries inside a still-closed per-minute window. The number was
// already in hand: the caller parses `err` three lines earlier and then discards it. Free-tier
// per-minute limits are the constraint this whole build is paced around (see the
// AUDIT_POOL_WIDTH note), so honouring the figure the API actually supplies is not cosmetic.
//
// The server hint is a FLOOR, not a licence to retry sooner than our own curve would, so the
// two are combined with max(). Capped at 60s so a pathological value cannot hang a run.
function geminiRetryDelayMs(err,headers,attempt){
  const exp=Math.pow(2,attempt+1)*1000+Math.random()*1000;
